  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>While the infinite reaches of the star-speckled night sky contain the answers to many mysteries, most primordial dancers simply forget what they were told the instant they stop dancing. Though you're not much better, you do remember some things.</p>\n<p><strong>Prerequisite:</strong> Dances class feature, know the behold the infinite dance,Wis 12</p>\n<p><strong>Benefit:</strong> Whenever you cease performing the behold the infinite dance, choose any number of spell-like abilities gained through the use of that dance's active abilities whose spell levels add up to 3 or less. Treat 0th-level spells as though their spell level were 1/2 for the purpose of this feat. You retain the ability to cast these spells even though you are no longer performing. If you once again begin performing the behold the infinite dance, gain some new spell-like abilities, and then cease to perform again, you must choose your spells to retain from the full list of spells gained in this manner, including those retained from a previous performance.</p>\n<p>Whenever you replenish the daily duration of the behold the infinite dance, all spell-like abilities retained by Infinity Retained are lost.</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/primordial-dancer-feats#toc9\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
      "instructions": ""
    },
